  "details": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * kernel: mm/damon/ops-common: handle extreme intervals in damon_hot_score() (CVE-2026-64458)\n  * kernel: crypto: ecc - Fix carry overflow in vli multiplication (CVE-2026-64313)\n  * kernel: ALSA: usx2y: us144mkii: fix work UAF on disconnect (CVE-2026-64491)\n  * kernel: Bluetooth: bpa10x: avoid OOB read of revision string in bpa10x_setup() (CVE-2026-64549)\n  * kernel: fscrypt: Add missing superblock check in find_or_insert_direct_key() (CVE-2026-68148)\n  * kernel: sunrpc: harden rq_procinfo lifecycle to prevent double-free (CVE-2026-72220)\n  * kernel: selinux: avoid sk_socket dereference in selinux_sctp_bind_connect() (CVE-2026-72242)\n  * kernel: net: ipip: require CAP_NET_ADMIN in the device netns for changelink (CVE-2026-72053)\n  * kernel: scsi: target: Bound PR-OUT TransportID parsing to the received buffer (CVE-2026-72084)\n  * kernel: RDMA/bnxt_re: Free SRQ toggle page after firmware teardown (CVE-2026-72500)\n  * kernel: NFSD: Handle layout stid in nfsd4_drop_revoked_stid() (CVE-2026-74316)\n  * kernel: RDMA/bnxt_re: Free CQ toggle page after firmware teardown (CVE-2026-72499)\n  * kernel: perf/core: Fix group leader use-after-free after sibling detach (CVE-2026-74637)\n  * kernel: sunrpc: defer rq_argp and rq_resp free until after RCU grace period (CVE-2026-89545)\n  * kernel: nfsd: RCU-protect cl_cb_session to fix use-after-free on session teardown (CVE-2026-89708)\n  * kernel: nfsd: validate sockaddr length per family in listener_set (CVE-2026-89700)\n  * kernel: NFSD: check truncate permission under inode lock (CVE-2026-89713)\n  * kernel: NFSv4/pnfs: key the data server cache on the NFS version (CVE-2026-90102)\n  * kernel: arm64: ptrace: Keep 'orig_x0' in-sync with x0 on syscall entry (CVE-2026-90347)\n  * kernel: Bluetooth: hci_conn: fix the SCO setup context lifetime (CVE-2026-90255)\n  * kernel: RDMA/bnxt_re: Clear VM_MAYWRITE on DBR/toggle page mmap (CVE-2026-92495)\n  * kernel: nfsd: convert nfsd_net boolean flags to unsigned long flags word (CVE-2026-93221)\n  * kernel: svcrdma: Fix unmatched rn_unregister on failed accept (CVE-2026-93224)\n  * kernel: i3c: master: Fix device_register() error path (CVE-2026-93283)\n  * kernel: vxlan: mdb: Fix use-after-free in vxlan_mdb_flush() (CVE-2026-93250)\n  * kernel: btrfs: fix use-after-free on reloc root after error in insert_dirty_subvol() (CVE-2026-93800)\n  * kernel: btrfs: tree-checker: validate names in ROOT_REF and ROOT_BACKREF (CVE-2026-97415)\n  * kernel: btrfs: tree-checker: validate INODE_REF's namelen (CVE-2026-93813)\n  * kernel: scsi: qla2xxx: Unlink NVMe unsol ctx before freeing on LS reject error (CVE-2026-97528)\n  * kernel: kernel: arbitrary code execution via out-of-bounds stack access in scsi_cdl_enable() (CVE-2026-98232)\n  * kernel: futex: Also allocate private hash on vfork() (CVE-2026-98281)\n  * kernel: tcp: prevent collapsing skbs across boundary in rtx queue (CVE-2026-98549)\n  * sandboxed-containers: kernel: systemd-gpt-auto-generator: Guest Data Leakage in Confidential Computing (Sandboxed Containers) (CVE-2026-121876)\n  * kernel: cipso: adjust cached option offsets when removing CIPSO (CVE-2026-99064)\n  * kernel: net/sched: fix use-after-free in __tcf_action_put() (CVE-2026-99167)\n  * kernel: kernel: Privilege escalation via reference counter wrap in io_uring (CVE-2026-99227)\n  * kernel: kernel: Denial of Service via race condition in TCP socket lookup (CVE-2026-99288)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * [rhel-10.3.z]Booting slowdown / soft lockups when booting VM with large GPU BAR [rhel-10.3.z] (JIRA:RHEL-253945)\n  * backport 2 virtio-net big packet commits, to fix severe performance degration regression [rhel-10.3.z] (JIRA:RHEL-255941)\n  * Fix pending kernel issues for L1VH GA - Kernel [rhel-10.3.z] (JIRA:RHEL-274964)\n  * Critical Bug Fixes for customer issues with lpfc [rhel-10.3.z] (JIRA:RHEL-286168)\n  * [RHEL-10.3.z] RDMA/bnxt_re: Backport security fixes (JIRA:RHEL-300139)\n  * [AlmaLinux 10.3] drm/ttm: Bump TTM_NUM_MEM_TYPES to 10 (JIRA:RHEL-307271)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
